WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.960
As far as this trip goes.

00:02.660 --> 00:08.914
Fifty-three million light-years, to the black hole in M87, the first one ever photographed.

00:09.364 --> 00:15.348
The map goes further, to a quasar's black hole nearly eleven billion light-years out.

00:15.798 --> 00:24.933
It shows more than a hundred thousand of the stars Gaia has measured, and every confirmed planet around another star whose distance is known.

00:25.383 --> 00:27.217
The rest is out there.

00:27.667 --> 00:30.197
We have not drawn what we cannot place.
